A||N||4||cowans||What shifter cables for stretched Kit???||||6||
Z||000000||cowans||09-19-2000||09:12 AM||||I was wondering what shifter cables have been used when stretching a fiero frame 7 inches. Anybody with any hints? thanks, Sandy||||reg||6
Z||000001||rockcrawl||09-19-2000||05:15 PM||||I'm working on a car with a 7" stretch also. I haven't completely decided which trans I'm going to use, but I will also need longer cable(s). There's something called a Morse cable that is used in auto racing and boating that should work great. They come in lots of different lengths. Capt Ron said he used a 6' marine cable to replace a bad cable on his Fiero and it shifted like a new car. All that is required to mount them is some minor mods to the brackets. <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jegs.com</A>  sells cables by TCI, B&M, and Hurst.  <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000002||dman||09-19-2000||07:32 PM||||Hello everyone.<P>Are you sure you need new cables? I've got a Testarossa that's stretched that much. It has the stock v6 auto in it right now (which I'm gonna replace sometime) but I did not need to replace any cables or wires for the stretch. The only items that needed replacement were the two lower coolant hoses.<P>Which cable is too short? The shift or select cable? Which transmission (Isuzu, 5spd Getrag, 4spd Muncie) are you using?<BR>If (when?) I replace the v6 and auto trannie, I'm gonna face the same issues as you.<P>BTW, how is the Testarossa project coming along rockcrawl?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||09-19-2000||08:30 PM||||I won't be making any progress on my Ferraricar until after my new house/garage is done next year and I get moved in there. For now it's just collecting dust while I plan and dream. Now that you mention it, the stock fiero auto shift cable does reach the 440t4 trans I have in the car now, even with the 7" stretch. The problem is that it has the exact opposite pattern of a Fiero trans and there's no room to just flip the arm, I need to loop the cable around and bring it in from the rear. I wonder how others get around this problem when installing this trans with 3800s etc.. Anyway, the more I think about it, the more I want a 5spd in the Ferrari. It'll cost me a bit more, but I think it's worth it. <P>I looked at my 86 GT (muncie 4spd) and there's no way you'd stretch the car 7" without installing longer cables. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||7
Z||000004||cowans||09-20-2000||08:22 AM||||Thanks to all of you who responded. I was speaking with Rodney Dickman yesterday afternoon and he suggested using the 5-speed Getrag select cables(approx 73" long). Yes Rockcrawl, the 85 4-speed Muncie(that I'm using) comes in around 63". I ordered 2 from Rodney. Sandy ||||reg||6
